-- 0049 — Sahaba Club's own archive: 17 events, Aug 2023 – Mar 2024
-- ============================================================
--
-- Until now not one event in the database was organized by Sahaba Club. The
-- Events Hub — "events created by Sahaba Club or our partners" — had nothing
-- to show, and the partners section had no relationships to draw on. This is
-- the club's back catalogue, from the workbook Ahmed supplied.
--
-- ⚠ GENERATED by tools/generate-archive-events-seed.mjs from "Old Events.xlsx".
-- Do not hand-edit the block below — re-run the generator. Nine of these rows
-- carry Arabic titles or Arabic descriptions, where a transcription slip would
-- be invisible in review and would ship a wrong title onto a live page. The
-- generator also refuses to emit at all if any row would collide with a live
-- event, because 0048's unique index would abort the import.
--
-- ============================================================
-- Three things decided here, all of them stated rather than assumed
-- ============================================================
--
-- **Sahaba Club is a co-organizer on ALL seventeen.** Ahmed confirmed the
-- whole workbook is the club's own archive. Where the file names somebody else
-- — Microsoft, IEEE, Google DevFest, Aqua Energy Expo — that organizer is
-- added ALONGSIDE and marked `is_lead`, so their logo leads the card and the
-- club is still correctly recorded as a co-host. This is exactly the case that
-- made organizer a table in 0048: one row's organizer is literally
-- "Microsoft & Sahaba Club", and a single column would have had to discard one
-- of two true answers.
--
-- **"Ahmed Abdel Razek" means Sahaba Club.** Three rows record the founder's
-- name where later rows record the club's. Confirmed by Ahmed rather than
-- guessed — rewriting the attribution on somebody's own history is not a
-- judgement call to make quietly.
--
-- ⚠ **TIMES ARE READ AS UTC+04 (Gulf).** The workbook records wall-clock times
-- with no timezone at all. The club is UAE-registered, so Gulf time is the
-- reasonable reading — but `starts_at` is a timestamptz and storing one means
-- committing to an offset. For events three years past, displayed as dates,
-- an hour changes nothing visible. If these were actually run on Cairo time
-- (UTC+2) every stored instant is two hours late and one UPDATE fixes it.
--
-- ---- What is deliberately absent -------------------------------------------
--
-- **No images.** The workbook has none, so all seventeen land with
-- `image_url` null and will fall back to the default square artwork. They are
-- the first candidates for the upload control being built next.
--
-- **`mode` is 'Online' on every row and `country` is null.** These were
-- webinars. ⚠ Two are probably not: "Sahaba Club @ GosTech - IEEE BU" runs
-- five hours from 10:00 at a university, and the Google DevFest session reads
-- like an in-person conference slot. Both are flagged in the verification
-- block rather than guessed at here — marking an event In-Person also means
-- claiming a country, and inventing a venue is worse than leaving it open.
--
-- **16 of 17 carry a recording.** On-Demand was dropped as a tab, but these
-- YouTube links are the club's back catalogue and the event page offers them.

-- GENERATED by tools/generate-archive-events-seed.mjs from "Old Events.xlsx"
